Incumbent Democrat [[Chris Dodd]] won re-election for a fifth term, beating Republican [[Jack Orchulli]], CEO and co-founder of a [[Michael Kors]]'s apparel company.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ourcampaigns.com/CandidateDetail.html?CandidateID=34855|title=Our Campaigns - Candidate - Jack Orchulli|website=www.ourcampaigns.com|access-date=20 December 2017}}</ref>

Chris Dodd was one of the most powerful senators in Congress. In the election cycle, he raised over $7 million. His top five contributors were [[Bear Stearns]], [[Citigroup]], [[National Westminster Bank]], [[Lehman Brothers]], and [[Goldman Sachs]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.opensecrets.org/members-of-congress/summary?cid=N00000581&cycle=2004 |title=Sen. Chris Dodd - Campaign Finance Summary |website=[[OpenSecrets]]}}</ref>

Republican nominee Jack Orchulli ran as a fiscal conservative and social moderate.{{Citation needed|date=February 2010}} He broke ranks with his party on [[gay marriage]] and [[abortion]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2016-04-12 |title=Jack Orchulli of Darien Announces He'll Run Against U.S. Sen. Richard Blumenthal |url=https://darienite.com/jack-orchulli-of-darien-announces-hell-run-against-u-s-sen-richard-blumenthal-9258 |access-date=2024-06-01 |website=Darienite |language=en-US}}</ref> That put him on the same side as most voters in the [[blue state]] of Connecticut.{{Citation needed|date=February 2010}} He often talked about a "broken education system." He argued that Dodd had not done anything in his 30 years in Congress to fix such issues as traffic problems in [[Fairfield County, Connecticut|Fairfield County]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/courant/access/725612191.html?dids=725612191:725612191&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT&type=current&date=Oct+28,+2004&author=JACK+DOLAN;+Courant+Staff+Writer&pub=Hartford+Courant&desc=OUTSIDER+TAKES+ON+SENATE+HEAVYWEIGHT+;+NEWCOMER+JACK+ORCHULLI+KNOCKS+INCUMBENT+CHRISTOPHER+DODD%27S+30+YEARS+OF+EXPERIENCE&pqatl=google|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120715070146/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/courant/access/725612191.html?dids=725612191:725612191&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT&type=current&date=Oct+28,+2004&author=JACK+DOLAN;+Courant+Staff+Writer&pub=Hartford+Courant&desc=OUTSIDER+TAKES+ON+SENATE+HEAVYWEIGHT+;+NEWCOMER+JACK+ORCHULLI+KNOCKS+INCUMBENT+CHRISTOPHER+DODD'S+30+YEARS+OF+EXPERIENCE&pqatl=google|archive-date=July 15, 2012|title=The Hartford Courant article archive - OUTSIDER TAKES ON SENATE HEAVYWEIGHT|website=pqasb.pqarchiver.com|access-date=20 December 2017}}</ref>

Orchulli launched a statewide TV ad campaign in September, as he spent over $1.1 million and pledged to spend "whatever it takes" if polls showed he was gaining ground on Dodd.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/courant/access/715543501.html?dids=715543501:715543501&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT&type=current&date=Oct+16,+2004&author=JACK+DOLAN;+Courant+Staff+Writer&pub=Hartford+Courant&desc=DODD+REPORTS+$3.3+MILLION;+ORCHULLI,+$28,000&pqatl=google|title=The Hartford Courant article archive - DODD REPORTS $3.3 MILLION|website=pqasb.pqarchiver.com|access-date=20 December 2017|archive-date=25 October 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121025111824/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/courant/access/715543501.html?dids=715543501:715543501&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT&type=current&date=Oct+16,+2004&author=JACK+DOLAN%3B+Courant+Staff+Writer&pub=Hartford+Courant&desc=DODD+REPORTS+$3.3+MILLION%3B+ORCHULLI,+$28,000&pqatl=google}}</ref>

